Certainly! Here's a more comprehensive list of triad chords and their respective names:

1. Major Triad (C): Root, Major Third, Perfect Fifth - C E G
2. Minor Triad (Cm): Root, Minor Third, Perfect Fifth - C E♭ G
3. Augmented Triad (Caug or C+): Root, Major Third, Augmented Fifth - C E G♯
4. Diminished Triad (Cdim or Co): Root, Minor Third, Diminished Fifth - C E♭ G♭

Extended and altered triads:

5. Suspended 2nd Triad (Csus2): Root, Major Second, Perfect Fifth - C D G
6. Suspended 4th Triad (Csus4): Root, Perfect Fourth, Perfect Fifth - C F G
7. Major Seventh Triad (Cmaj7): Root, Major Third, Perfect Fifth, Major Seventh - C E G B
8. Minor Seventh Triad (Cmin7 or Cm7): Root, Minor Third, Perfect Fifth, Minor Seventh - C E♭ G B♭
9. Augmented Major Seventh Triad (Cmaj7♯5): Root, Major Third, Augmented Fifth, Major Seventh - C E G♯ B
10. Half-Diminished Triad (Cø7 or Cm7♭5): Root, Minor Third, Diminished Fifth, Minor Seventh - C E♭ G♭ B♭

Inversions of the basic triads:

11. First Inversion Major Triad (C/E): Third, Fifth, Root - E G C
12. Second Inversion Major Triad (C/G): Fifth, Root, Third - G C E
13. First Inversion Minor Triad (Cm/E♭): Third, Fifth, Root - E♭ G C
14. Second Inversion Minor Triad (Cm/G): Fifth, Root, Third - G C E♭

Altered and extended variations:

15. Dominant Seventh Triad (C7): Root, Major Third, Perfect Fifth, Minor Seventh - C E G B♭
16. Dominant Seventh Suspended 4th Triad (C7sus4): Root, Perfect Fourth, Perfect Fifth, Minor Seventh - C F G B♭
17. Dominant Seventh Sharp Ninth Triad (C7♯9): Root, Major Third, Perfect Fifth, Minor Seventh, Sharp Ninth - C E G B♭ D♯
18. Major Sixth Triad (C6): Root, Major Third, Perfect Fifth, Major Sixth - C E G A
19. Minor Sixth Triad (Cm6): Root, Minor Third, Perfect Fifth, Major Sixth - C E♭ G A
20. Minor Major Seventh Triad (CmMaj7): Root, Minor Third, Perfect Fifth, Major Seventh - C E♭ G B
21. Major Ninth Triad (Cmaj9): Root, Major Third, Perfect Fifth, Major Seventh, Major Ninth - C E G B D
22. Minor Ninth Triad (Cmin9): Root, Minor Third, Perfect Fifth, Minor Seventh, Major Ninth - C E♭ G B♭ D

These are some common triads and their names. Keep in mind that there are even more variations and extensions possible in music theory, depending on the context and the specific chords used in a piece of music.

